<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uslar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uslar is a small town in the Solling hills of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gottingen">Göttingen</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it belonged to the Guelph Principality of Göttingen and later to Calenberg and the Electorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>. A market town for the surrounding forest villages, it lived from farming, forestry and small industries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uslar.jpg" alt="Uslar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uwe Barghaan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uslar_Lange_Str_2012.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
